  /* ---- Read-along ----------------------------------------------------
     The highlighted-paragraph and floating-control styles below reach
     outside this component (the §-anchors live in the page templates,
     the float is positioned against the sticky header and each
     section's own .margin-col), so they're written as :global(). */

  /* Once JS has wired up cues, narrated anchors become click-to-seek
     targets — cursor only, no visual change, so unread paragraphs don't
     look different from read ones until they're actually read. */
  :global(body.audio-narr-ready [data-narr]) {
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Active-paragraph highlight: a padded box drawn AROUND the block, not
     on it — negative margin pulls the box out into the gutter by exactly
     the amount the matching padding adds back inside it, so the box's
     total footprint (and every character's on-screen position) is
     unchanged; a browser sanity check confirms zero shift on the first
     text node's getBoundingClientRect(). The red rule is an inset
     box-shadow at the box's own (now-expanded) left edge, so it lands
     14px (10px on phones) clear of the first glyph — box-shadow, not a
     real border, so it still never takes layout space. Text colour is
     untouched; the tint alone stays well clear of WCAG's 7:1 body-text
     contrast floor (measured, not just intended — see stage5/MANIFEST.md).
     One rule for every kind of narrated block — paragraphs, headings,
     figures, tables, stat strips, the watch gallery — so there's exactly
     one highlight treatment on the page, not a paragraph one and a
     "wide block" one. --paper-raised is the fallback for browsers
     without color-mix().

     The four box-model properties are !important: the zero-shift trick
     only cancels out exactly when margin and padding both apply in full,
     and several narrated elements (e.g. .standfirst) carry their own
     page-scoped margin-bottom whose Astro-scoped selector ties this
     rule's specificity — without !important that page rule wins the
     cascade tie and silently keeps the old margin-bottom, breaking the
     cancellation on that one edge (caught by a real getBoundingClientRect
     check, not assumed: the dek shifted -6px vertically until this was
     added). */
  :global([data-narr].is-reading) {
    margin-inline: -14px !important;
    padding-inline: 14px !important;
    margin-block: -6px !important;
    padding-block: 6px !important;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background-color: var(--paper-raised);
    background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--red) 7%, var(--paper));
    box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--red);
    transition: background-color 180ms var(--ease-draw), box-shadow 180ms var(--ease-draw);
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    :global([data-narr].is-reading) {
